DXVK patch 10 -- keep clip/cull SPIR-V capabilities and D3D9 caps coherent.

Apply after dxvk-patches/01-mali-d3d9-pipeline-compat.patch to DXVK-Sarek
commit 617958fe1cf2b10e06fa751d3e40bd765dcf2cc6. This is a source-only audit
candidate; it is not part of the FINALPLAY21 D3D9 DLL stage.

Patch 01 correctly suppresses ClipDistance/CullDistance declarations when the
Vulkan feature is unavailable, but enables each SPIR-V capability only from the
stage's output-plane count. Pixel-shader inputs and HS/DS/GS inputs can still
declare the builtin with no matching capability. Once the device feature is
enabled, enabling the capability for the module is legal even if a particular
stage ends up not using it; use that direct condition for every DXBC stage and
cover pixel-shader inputs as well.

On a device such as the RG353VS where shaderClipDistance is unavailable, also
report zero D3D9 user clip planes instead of accepting state that patch 01 must
drop. MGS2 has no SetClipPlane or D3DRS_CLIPPLANEENABLE call, so this is not a
flicker or performance candidate for this game.

